There is a bug in the polymorph routine.  The routine sets the number
of gems to be the same as the number of rocks, but does not recalculate
the weight of the pile, and the weight is left at 1.  When you drop *some*
of the pile, the weight is recalculated, and suddenly you can't carry
the remaining gems.  Your pack load went from 1 jade stone to 100 jade
stones and you collapsed.  If you drop the whole pile, the weight is not
recalculated, and you can pick the entire pile again.

Incidentally, there is another bug in the same routine.  When you
polymorph a wand, you get a fully charged wand, even if the previous
wand had 0 charges.  The following are the fixes for both of the
bugs.  You may not want to put the min() function in.  This prevents
the polymorphed wand from having more than a normal number of charges.


*** hack.zap.old	Sat Jan 18 18:22:31 1986
